    {
      "id": "claim_8ab2779446e94600828156c364276fbb",
      "statement": "Each issue delivery is routed by an ordered guard sequence in GitHubWebhookProcessor: only issues events with action opened, labeled, edited, or reopened whose issue is open and carries the case-insensitive label `feature` are processed; then an incomplete spec is commented and closed, and only a complete spec that also carries `ready-for-agent` is enqueued as an ImplementSpec job built from the payload's title and body. Push events bypass the queue and instead call git.SyncMainAsync inline in the webhook request.",
      "evidence": [
