    {
      "id": "claim_835a71c3ad354778819dce3a4ba38e53",
      "statement": "Sebastian enforces one process per repository: Git derives its working root from IHostEnvironment.ContentRootPath and throws at startup when that path is not the git top level, then parses `origin` into the instance's RepositoryIdentity; a job whose payload owner/repository does not match that identity throws in PrepareWorkspaceAsync (after admission) rather than being redirected, so a foreign-repository delivery appears only as a failed job log line.",
